.TH ASMSPEED 1 "2026-11-13" "asmspeed 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asmspeed \- terminal internet speed test written in x86-64 assembly
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B asmspeed
[\fB\-t\fR \fISECONDS\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Measures latency, download speed and upload speed against
speed.cloudflare.com over plain HTTP. Each direction runs over several
parallel TCP connections. A 2 second warm-up is not counted; the reported
speed is the average over the measured window that follows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t " " \fISECONDS\fR
Measure each direction for SECONDS seconds (1\-60, default 8).
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fIN\fR
Use N parallel connections (1\-8, default 4).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the server could not be reached, 2 on bad arguments.
.SH NOTES
Traffic is unencrypted HTTP and carries no personal data; the upload payload is zeros.
Results are in megabits per second (1 Mbps = 1,000,000 bits/s).
